{"kind":"assert","text":"C4 one-submit source proposal: a passed primary ActRef handles a primary-only race, but cannot cover the existing also/value-via race. That real witness moves target while primary now stays unchanged. A general one-submit guarantee needs the rendered subject-basis value. No source changed for this proposal.","body":{"cost":"Readonlyprojectionwritesnothing and neverfabricatesStoredDraftReturn. The explicit membercall must persistthebasis/capture actuallysubmitted in its oneapprovedDraftPortbatch beforeE4retain/sign, orrestart canroll backbasis. Preserveunrelated sparseexpected/fields, oldbasiswhenargumentabsent, no hiddennewestview/retry/secondsubmit/crossstoretransaction. PagehasnoC4callernow; futurecallerclosesoverrenderedvalueanddoesnotrereadlatestview. Existingrawprojector/preflight/helperprefixesremainimmutable/source-only.","decision":"Choose primary-only submit(slot,seen?:ActRef) with explicit also/open limitation, or complete rendered seen-basis for the general one-submit guarantee. I prefer complete explicit subject basis if the owner's no-extra-submit rule covers allrevision-moved races; one ActRef cannot honestly refresh unseen aliases. The same captured Form2scope/revision-moved occurrence must gate the optional branch; omitted preserves prior B0/B1+Explore path, null/wrongprimary shape-refuses, validstale usesrealExplore, movedagain givesgenuineForm1.","proposal":"# Pass the rendered primary ref to one explicit submit\n\nSource-only proposal under planner e2e2eb73afebd9c4f30551951741624cd182a68d. No C4 source change is authorized yet. The split/E2 request is outside this report.\n\nRecommend an explicit optional second value, `submit(slot, seen?)`, for the primary-row race described by the ruling. It can remove the extra submit when only that primary basis moved. **A single ActRef cannot remove the extra submit for every also-subject race.** The existing real value-slot-via witness demonstrates that limit. Planner should confirm the primary-only scope or choose the complete subject-value alternative below before code; do not silently refresh unseen expected keys.\n\n## Preserve Form 2 and zero background draft writes\n\nThe source history is ff578fef6bd964fc9a94bd060d1f91688599f6ad, corrected by481aac4e3481a57c712d4ecbba3ffc16226492a3: the normal race is A exploring at39, B recording40 before A reaches the scope, and the scope returning revision-moved. No Replica fault is implied. The former extra-submit path remains the fallback when the member supplies no new seen value.\n\nKeep current raw storage: ordinary request cause stays in actual custody; StoredDraftReturn holds only genuine local Explore movement. B1 and authored captures stay stored unchanged while read/feed/render/reload project Form2. No step writes the ordinary cause to DraftPort. No new cause-only raw arm or faux movement receipt appears. The new proposal changes only read-only view data and what a later explicit member submit may accept.\n\nIn CP4, extend only the public `returned.by:\"request\"` form with optional `now:ActRef`. Populate it only when the actual existing request Why is scope/revision-moved and the fixed Slot's primary exists in the same checked Replica cut used by that publication. Keep pending/entry/stopped/local-submitting priorities and M/C0/C1 occurrence rules. A local unsent cause or other refusal does not gain this field.\n\nConstruct the ref from actual recorded row identity/revision, `{name:row.id,seen:row.revision,assumes:[]}`. Do not use #compute's predicted pending rows. Current ClientView rows are recorded/predicted Row data, not already ActRow.ref; CP2 shows the existing exact recorded-ref construction. The loader can pass an owned optional primary ref into the pure projector alongside its existing evidence. That is one data member, not a read callback/evaluator or public Replica operation. The getter is deterministic on that publication's checked cut and performs no read/authentication request.\n\nIf no primary exists, omit now. Open acts and comments on:null have no primary; keep their cause-only form. A later feed may change this read-only now, but cannot update stored B1. `returned.by` remains the form discriminator; null/omission must never identify the form.\n\n## Concrete call and value grammar\n\nProposed signature, source text only:\n\n```ts\nsubmit\u003cK extends Kind\u003cD\u003e\u003e(\n  slot: Slot\u003cD,K\u003e,\n  seen?: ActRef,\n): Promise\u003cDraftCall\u003cstring\u003e\u003e;\n```\n\nA rendered page owns the exact values it renders:\n\n```ts\nconst shownSlot = shown.slot;\nconst shownSeen = shown.returned?.by === \"request\"\n  ? shown.returned.now\n  : undefined;\n// The native submit handler closes over these owned values.\nawait client.submit(shownSlot, shownSeen);\n```\n\nDo not reread client.view in the handler to find a newer ref after the member starts the gesture. This is a future C4 caller requirement; no current Page C4 caller exists. Copied/serialized ref values remain valid. No WeakMap brand, token, common cut or credential hides behind them.\n\nOwn Slot through accepted ownDraftSlot and seen through existing readDraftRef before awaiting. ActRef's exact grammar is `{name,seen,assumes}`: ItemName is numeric or `{output:{key,version}}`, Revision is numeric or `{after:{key,version}}`, and assumes is a list of Source values. Reuse this reader, not a second decoder. An actual projected now is recorded numeric data with empty assumes. Symbolic values supplied otherwise retain existing held-source/state handling; this proposal adds no materialization, Source lookup or permission.\n\n- **Omitted/undefined:** use the existing stored prospective B1 when present, otherwise the original sparse basis/captures. Explore that candidate normally. If it moved, return genuine Form1; do not replace absence with the current row.\n- **Explicit null:** shape error, not “use current”, absence or clearing. An open/no-primary act supplies no second value.\n- **Wrong name or no matching Slot primary:** shape mismatch before launching writes. Compare copied ItemName values canonically; never retarget the Slot/draft. A valid stale ref is not malformed: let real Explore judge it.\n- **Valid same-name ref:** accept only its explicit primary basis. It grants no authority or freshness. For a transition, its seen/assumes replaces the candidate primary capture/expected.on. Comments retain expectedKeys' rule that primary on supplies no expected.on. Do not infer revisions for other aliases from it.\n\nThe names-only Slot address stays kind+primary name+present top-level item-field names. It still ignores seen/assumes. Required refs, optional presence/default distinction, null rejection and all fixed item selectors remain unchanged. The extra value is explicit submit intent, so a newly constructed equal-address Slot with fresher refs alone still cannot overwrite first captures. Editable values, fact bytes, text and sparse omitted fields do not change.\n\n## Member-call basis transition and B1 cost\n\nBuild the submission candidate from the existing prospective B1 if one exists, then overlay only the explicitly supplied primary ref. Never restart from older B0 or use Explore.result.act, which may autofill an omitted key. Do not re-run edit defaults or recapture transitive subjects merely because the current feed has them.\n\nThe actual E4 retained act/version must contain this same candidate expected map. actVersion hashes expected; submitBoundAct owns its input and retains/signs that exact act through preview/builder checks. Do not route C4 through legacy #request, which derives expectedOf from current rows. No E4 authority/permission/signature API needs a new public parameter.\n\nThere is a durable-data cost: if the member explicitly accepts a new seen basis, later editing/submission must not roll back to the old stored basis after a refusal or restart. The submit's member-owned draft replacement must keep that adopted basis/capture and matching namedRefs while leaving unrelated fields/expected omissions unchanged. Retire an obsolete local movement marker only as part of this explicit call; never forge its movement/head to record the view ref. Genuine new Explore movement keeps the existing Form1 return path.\n\nDo not write first and blindly continue if the raw write rejects: a rejection may have persisted. Keep the existing uncertain-write error/actual-storage reconciliation and committed-key/close reporting. No rollback, reroll or cross-store transaction is claimed.\n\nTo retain the accepted one whole draft-batch write, compose the candidate in owned memory, perform the actual Explore, then let the existing member-call precondition path write either the genuine moved return or the accepted seen-basis adoption before E4 retains/signs. It must revalidate the actual displayed/raw occurrence and lifecycle at the approved boundary; this report does not invent the still-unwritten caller's lock choreography or another custody sweep. If that composition cannot preserve the accepted boundary, stop for root rather than add an unreviewed second write.\n\nThe required normal-basis adoption must satisfy store refinement: primary capture matches namedRefs.on; explicit by item refs retain their own captures; complete alias inventory and optional presence stay exact. Reuse the already owed Form1 prospective-basis composition, not a new default/selection algorithm. That composition and C4 submit are still unimplemented. This proposal does not claim an existing helper already performs it.\n\nActual Explore remains first. If the checked primary moved from the member's supplied seen value, return genuine Form1 from CP2 with no new ACT signing. If unchanged, the existing unavailable-authority/source result still does not block ordinary Native submission; do not manufacture permission from now. The scope may still refuse a later race. There is no retry loop, second hidden Explore or automatic second submit.\n\n## The multiple-subject limit is concrete\n\nexpectedKeys includes transition on and unmarked also aliases. ActRef carries only one item's revision; its assumes contains retained Source assumptions, not an alias→revision map. Slot exposes primary and explicit top-level item selectors, but derived via/one/local-fact subjects can lie outside those refs. RefusalReason revision-moved gives no typed alias; judge.ts396–399 embeds the alias in human detail, which must not become a parser protocol.\n\nThe accepted real selection journey captures touch with expected.on and expected.target. It then records revise-target, asserts anchor revision unchanged, and receives genuine movement with `now` equal to that unchanged anchor ref while subjects.target has the new target revision. Passing that primary now cannot change expected.target honestly. A primary-only submit must still return Form1 in this case, preserving all unrelated sparse basis. A comment with moved also may have a primary that contributes no expected.on; an open act can have moved also with now:null. None admits a hidden “refresh everything” rule.\n\nIf the owner's one-submit requirement includes these races, the complete alternative is one optional owned **seen-basis value**, containing nullable primary plus the per-expected-alias present/absent selections from the rendered checked cut. It can reuse the existing DraftSelection grammar and shared selectDraftSubjects identity resolver, but must carry an explicit legal omission/undetermined treatment and preserve the original authored sparse act. The view would need that complete value, not only now. Submit would apply only those explicitly passed selections and then Explore; moved-again still produces genuine Form1.\n\nThat alternative adds more public view/input data and a closed input/refinement helper; it cannot masquerade as one ActRef or use DraftMovement, since no Explore decided the read-only view's selections. It also needs exact same-name/selector consistency and capture/refinement review before code. This report proposes no new schema implementation. Planner should choose the guarantee rather than infer approval from the primary-only rule.\n\n## Smaller alternatives do not remove these costs safely\n\nImplicitly using the latest Replica on every submit would sign on a basis the member did not pass. Reinterpreting the ordinary Slot argument's seen values would break the accepted equal-address/no-rebase rule. Internally doing the old moved-return submit and its following submit without another member action would accept a newly computed basis the member never saw. Background capture/write violates the standing rule. An explicit new edit-basis call followed by submit would add a public operation and would not be smaller than the optional seen argument.\n\nFor the primary-only guarantee, `submit(slot,seen?)` is the smallest explicit value handoff I found. It still owes durable accepted-basis composition; skipping that storage issue merely hides a restart regression.\n\n## Existing witness extensions and source cost\n\nExtend the already planned actual C4 draft-owner 39→40 race case, not a new synthetic matrix. Use real signed/judged entries and the existing causal gate between local Explore and destination judgment. Obtain the real scope revision-moved refusal, then show the read-only Form2 now while raw DraftPort bytes/write counts remain unchanged. Pass a JSON-copied seen value from that rendered view once; with no intervening movement require one new actual authorization/signature/submission and genuine acceptance, with the adopted basis preserved across reload. Count read-session authentication separately from ACT signatures.\n\nIn the same journey's moved-again branch, record the next actual revision after capturing shownSeen but before the next Explore. Require real Form1, zero additional ACT signing, original editable values preserved and no hidden retry. Keep existing assertions, barriers and deadlines. The existing real selection journey remains the precise multi-ref counterexample; extend the later method owner only after planner chooses its policy. Its current raw bridge case cannot prove submit persistence or E4 retention.\n\nLikely C4 source work: request-form type/projector input+owned now output; submit preflight using readDraftRef; original-sparse-candidate/accepted-basis composition; the existing ScopeClient submit preconditions and E4 handoff; the existing actual draft-owner race witness; and a short how-to update replacing the old mandatory extra-submit wording within the chosen guarantee. No raw request-cause arm, marker decoder change, kernel, grant, Native Answer, Source materializer, transport, session API or public Explore operation is proposed.\n\nCurrent Page code does not call C4 slot/edit/submit. Existing data.ts/retained-editor-data.ts submit signed handles through a different retained editor. Do not edit that protected Page lifecycle or bind dap-ui-sdk for this proposal. A later real C4 Page caller must pass the rendered values at its native gesture boundary; its exact path, producer/browser/model obligations and validation remain future source review, not included work.\n\n## Decision requested\n\nApprove the optional primary seen-ref route with its explicit also/open limitation, or require the complete rendered seen-basis value for a general one-submit guarantee. Confirm the submit member-call's accepted-basis persistence/composition cost before code. All current C4 checkpoints remain immutable, source-only and UNRUN; no API or caller implementation follows from this proposal.\n","scope_clarification":"# Limit the new seen argument to the returned-request route\n\nThe proposal's optional seen branch applies only to the same captured draft occurrence that is actually in ordinary Form2 with scope/revision-moved. It is not a generic rebase operation for a fresh editing draft, another key, local unsent cause, or an existing Form1 movement. The member caller must confirm that eligibility from its accepted finite custody observations and normal occurrence preconditions before launching its write. A current pending/entry/newer editor still has the existing taken priority. No value keeps the ordinary existing submit path.\n\nReferences remain copied values, not proof that a person saw a particular page or a private view token. This eligibility check relates the explicit input to the actual draft/custody occurrence; it grants no authority. Exact existing state/taken/shape payload mapping remains a source-implementation review obligation, not a new stop vocabulary.\n\nThis narrows the generic “valid same-name ref” wording in PROPOSAL.md to the actual Form2 route requested by e2e2eb73. The multiple-subject limitation and durable accepted-basis composition cost remain unchanged. No source or frozen checkpoint changed.\n","source":"Root FULLREAD complete PROPOSAL.md14073B SHAb3d58f4ba62e44b39b26760df52275061437bd295af2f0a28224698f27af42de and1226B clarification SHA32ae0a5cf56c989b12c58cdebf990fe5cdd8058f81369a8e984194ad02796032 in /private/tmp/artroom-c4-one-submit-source-proposal-20261116. Actual source bindings1ea43560e4cacc96aadedc4fd887adfa3c67ca2631da58bd99c31e5717ea25ec. No API/code/test/runtime change.","to":"planner"}}